---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Resources
permalink: /resources/
description: "Study notes, diagrams and free step-by-step tools (OR Lab and Stats Lab) for B.B.A. students, from the papers Inigo Papu Vinodhan teaches at St. Joseph's College."
pageScript: /assets/list-filter.js
---
<div class="wrap page">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">For students</p>
    <h1>Resources</h1>
    <p class="lead">Study notes with diagrams, and two sets of free step-by-step tools, OR Lab and Stats Lab, from the B.B.A. papers I teach. Use them, print them and pass them on.</p>
    <span class="head-motif">{% include "motifs/notes.svg" %}</span>
  </header>

  <section class="notes-section" aria-labelledby="notes-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="notes-title">Study notes</h2>
      <p class="section-note" id="notes-count" aria-live="polite">{{ collections.resources.length }} notes, newest first</p>
    </div>
    {#- Search and area filter: shown only when scripts run (without them every note is listed). Kept in ?area= and ?q= -#}
    <div class="list-tools" data-list-filter data-items=".note-grid > li" data-param="area" data-count="#notes-count" data-empty="#notes-empty" data-noun="note,notes">
      <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="Show notes by area">
        <button type="button" class="chip" data-value="all" aria-pressed="true">All <span>{{ collections.resources.length }}</span></button>
        {% for a in cv.teaching %}{% set inArea = collections.resources | byArea(a) %}<button type="button" class="chip" data-value="{{ a.id }}" aria-pressed="false"{% if not inArea.length %} disabled{% endif %}>{{ a.area }} <span>{{ inArea.length }}</span></button>{% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% set searchLabel = "Search the notes" %}{% set searchHint = "Search notes…" %}{% include "list-search.njk" %}
    </div>
    <ul class="note-grid">
      {% for item in collections.resources %}
        {% set c = item.data.course | course(cv.teaching) %}
        <li class="note-card" data-value="{{ c.areaId }}" data-search="{{ item.data.title }} {{ item.data.description }} {{ c.title }} {{ (item.data.keywords or []) | join(' ') }}">
          <div class="note-media">{% set d = item.data %}{% set decor = true %}{% include "media.njk" %}</div>
          <div class="note-body">
            <p class="card-meta"><span class="tag">{{ c.title }}</span>{% if c.sem %}<span>Semester {{ c.sem }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
            <h3><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a></h3>
            {% if item.data.description %}<p>{{ item.data.description }}</p>{% endif %}
          </div>
        </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <div class="list-empty" id="notes-empty" hidden>
      <p>No study notes match that yet.</p>
      <button type="button" class="chip">Show all notes</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="notes-section" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="tools-title">{{ orlab.name }}</h2>
      <p class="section-note">{{ orlab.tools | dictsort | length }} free tools for {{ orlab.paper }}, by unit</p>
    </div>
    <p class="tools-intro">Enter a problem from your textbook or class, and each tool works it out step by step, the way you would by hand, so you can check your own working.</p>
    <ul class="tool-list">
      {% for u in orlab.units %}{% for slug in u.tools %}
        <li><a href="/tools/{{ slug }}/"><span class="tool-unit">Unit {{ u.no }}</span><span class="tool-name">{{ orlab.tools[slug].title }}</span></a></li>
      {% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="tools-more"><a href="/tools/">What each tool does, and how to use them</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="notes-section" aria-labelledby="stats-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="stats-title">{{ statlab.name }}</h2>
      <p class="section-note">{{ statlab.tools | dictsort | length }} free tools for {{ statlab.paper }}, by unit</p>
    </div>
    <p class="tools-intro">The same idea for the mathematics and statistics paper: enter a problem and see every step of the working.</p>
    <ul class="tool-list">
      {% for u in statlab.units %}{% for slug in u.tools %}
        <li><a href="/tools/{{ slug }}/"><span class="tool-unit">Unit {{ u.no }}</span><span class="tool-name">{{ statlab.tools[slug].title }}</span></a></li>
      {% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="tools-more"><a href="/tools/stats/">What each tool does, and how to use them</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="syllabus" aria-labelledby="syllabus-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="syllabus-title">Papers I teach</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="area-grid">
      {% for a in cv.teaching %}
        <section class="area" id="{{ a.id }}" aria-labelledby="area-{{ a.id }}">
          <h3 id="area-{{ a.id }}">{{ a.area }}</h3>
          <ul class="area-courses">
            {% for c in a.courses %}
              {% set notes = collections.resources | byCourse(c.slug) %}
              <li{% if notes.length or c.slug == "operations-research" or c.slug == "business-mathematics-statistics" %} class="has-notes"{% endif %}>
                <span class="area-course">{{ c.title }}</span>
                {% for n in notes %}<a class="area-note" href="{{ n.url }}">{{ n.data.title }}</a>{% endfor %}
                {% if c.slug == "operations-research" %}<a class="area-note" href="/tools/">{{ orlab.name }}: step-by-step tools</a>{% endif %}
                {% if c.slug == "business-mathematics-statistics" %}<a class="area-note" href="/tools/stats/">{{ statlab.name }}: step-by-step tools</a>{% endif %}
              </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </section>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {% set other = collections.resources | otherCourses(cv.teaching) %}
  {% if other.length %}
    <section class="cv-section">
      <h2>More resources</h2>
      {% set list = other %}{% include "entry-list.njk" %}
    </section>
  {% endif %}
</div>

